**Responsibilities:**  

To be the in\\-charge of the hospital laboratory to manage the day\\-to\\-day operations;



To plan, lead, manage and co\\-ordinate all laboratory activities, including supplies and inventory management;



To establish and maintain clinical and service guidelines and standards;



To advise on the choices of appropriate tests and interpretation of results;



To monitor and improve the work process, where appropriate;



To maintain effective communications with hospital colleagues, as well as external clients such as other medical centres and laboratories;



To manage and monitor the applications of new technologies, where appropriate;



To act as the Quality Controller, Document Controller, and Safety Officer in the laboratory;



To monitor and optimize the departmental finance;



To participate into and lead the establishment of quality assurance and audit system and tools to ensure a safe and effective service;



To comply with the accreditation requirements of the Hong Kong Laboratory Accreditation Scheme (HOKLAS);



To act as the “Laboratory Director” for the purpose of the accreditation by HOKLAS in the hospital; and



Other duties as assigned by the hospital management as and when required.



**Requirements:**  

Master’s degree (or equivalent qualification) in medical sciences or related subjects and obtaining a qualification by examination in medical sciences or related subjects accepted by the Medical Laboratory Technologist (MLT) Board for registration as Part I technologists;



A minimal of eight years of relevant medical testing experience, three of which shall be at a supervisory level;



Part I Registration of Medical Laboratory Technologist with a valid practicing certificate issued by the HKMLT Board;



Experience in Total Laboratory Automation (TLA) may be an advantage;



Any other duties as assigned from time to time by the hospital management;



Good command of written and spoken English and Chinese;



**Closing date for application:** 30 November 2025\\.



