**FINANCE OFFICE**
**Senior Finance Manager / Finance Manager (Special Projects) (23241256\\)**
**Responsibilities:**
* Lead finance transformation initiatives, collaborating with cross\\-functional teams to ensure successful implementation;
* Manage all aspects of financial planning and analysis, financial accounting, and capital project monitoring;
* Evaluate and improve existing financial processes and policies, identifying areas for enhancement;
* Collaborate as a strategic partner with various departments and academic units, providing financial advice to support decision\\-making processes;
* Continuously improve the efficiency of financial reporting processes, including month\\-end and annual closing, management reporting, budgeting exercises, and the fixed assets register, by implementing best practices and automation tools;
* Work closely with cross\\-functional teams to ensure accurate, timely, and value\\-added reporting;
* Develop and maintain frameworks for financial and management reporting; experience in capital project accounting is advantageous;
* Prepare the annual budget, manage budgetary control, and participate in digital transformation projects and process improvement initiatives; and
* Perform tasks as assigned by supervisors.






**Requirements:**
* A degree holder with membership of a recognised professional accounting body;
* Minimum 10 years’ experience in financial accounting and management reporting, preferably sizeable organisations (those with less work experience will be considered as Manager);
* In\\-depth knowledge of accounting principles; detail\\-oriented, independent, responsible and proactive in seeking solutions;
* Excellent project management and communication skills, both written and spoken English and Chinese;
* Ability to meet tight deadlines and work effectively under pressure;
* Proactive and strong analytical skills and collaboration abilities; Good proficiency in computer literacy such as Oracle, Hyperion, Power BI; and
* Prior working experience in audit firms will be an advantage.






 Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend a proficiency test.




 The initial appointment will be offered on a fixed\\-term contract of 2 to 3 years. Re\\-appointment thereafter is subject to mutual agreement and availability of funding.




*Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience.*
**Application Procedure:**
 Applicants are invited to submit their applications at the HKBU e\\-Recruitment System. Those who are not invited for an interview 8 weeks after submission of applications may consider their applications unsuccessful. Details of the University's Personal Information Collection Statement can be found at https://hro.hkbu.edu.hk/en/worklife\\-at\\-hkbu/employee\\-favourable\\-environment.html\\#privacy\\-policy.




 The University reserves the right not to make an appointment for the post advertised, and the appointment will be made according to the terms and conditions applicable at the time of offer.




**Review of applications is ongoing until the position is filled.**

The West Kowloon Cultural District Authority welcomes exceptional talent with a passion to realise the vision and mission of making the West Kowloon Cultural District a prime local and international destination for arts, culture and entertainment.




**You Will Be Responsible For**
* assisting the Manager, Finance to prepare the group financial reporting and consolidation for WKCDA and its subsidiaries;
* preparing financial and management reports and analysis on a timely and accurate basis with illuminating and succinct commentaries;
* consolidating, reconciling and validating financial information from multiple sources to develop financial forecasts, business and corporate plans, control and analysis to ensure the business activities are conducted in accordance with budget parameters, cost guidelines, reporting principles and with good governance;
* streamlining work processes on reporting and institute control procedures to ensure effective, efficient and timely reporting;
* assisting the Manager, Finance to compile the fixed assets register and oversee the bookkeeping of fixed assets in the ERP and internal control of fixed asset management;
* supporting the Head, Financial Reporting and Manager, Finance to work on projects of new system implementation project; system enhancement and development, integrate financial information needs across the business unit, implement automation initiatives and digitisation transformation, drive continuous improvement in financial reporting and analysis as well as systems and processes; and
* performing other duties commensurate with the position of Assistant Manager, Finance and performing such services from time to time as WKCDA may reasonably direct.


**You Should**
* possess a recognised university degree with professional qualifications in Finance, Accounting or relevant discipline;
* possess a membership of the Hong Kong Institute of Certified Public Accountants or equivalent;
* have at least 5\\-7 years of relevant experience in finance, auditing or accounting, preferably gained in a multinational / large organisation;
* have a good understanding and be familiar with the public sector in Hong Kong will be a plus;
* have strong stakeholder management and leadership skills, sound judgment and strong ethics with impeccable integrity;
* have good knowledge in ERP systems, financial modelling, business controls and management reporting;
* have project leadership experience in system implementation, process automation, digital transformation, system maintenance or enhancement, system testing and end user training support is a plus;
* have good business acumen with strong analytical skills and critical thinking mindset;
* be detail\\-oriented while having the ability to think creatively and out of the box;
* be a good team spirit and a good financial advisor;
* be able to engage and communicate with multiple stakeholders;
* have excellent Excel and PowerPoint skills; and
* have excellent oral and written communication skills in both English and Chinese.


 For interested parties, please submit your application with detailed CV on or before following date. Applicants are encouraged to submit their applications as soon as possible. The review of applications will continue until post is filled.




